    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.dfs_postorder_nodes - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.dfs_postorder_nodes.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dfs_postorder_nodes()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List nodes in depth-first postorder.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dfs_postorder_nodes()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List nodes in depth-first postorder.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.dfs_postorder_nodes()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: List nodes in depth-first postorder.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nList nodes in depth-first postorder.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L65322-L65436){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.dfs_postorder_nodes(\n    source=None,\n    depth_limit=None,\n    mode=\"out\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![DFS postorder](../assets/graphs/dfs-postorder-nodes.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A seven-node tree searched depth-first from the root A (outlined). Numbered badges give the order nodes finish: D and E finish before their parent B, F and G before C, and the root A finishes last. The card lists D, E, B, F, G, C, A, beside the preorder A, B, D, E, C, F, G that dfs() returns.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nIn a depth-first search, a node is *finished* once every node below it has been\nexplored. Postorder lists nodes in the order they finish, so every node comes after\nall of its DFS descendants. This is the order to process a tree bottom-up (children\nbefore parents), and in a DAG, the reverse of the postorder is a topological order.\n`dfs()` gives the complementary preorder, the order nodes are first reached.\n\nWith `source=None` (default), the search covers every node, restarting from unvisited\nnodes in ID order. Neighbors are explored in edge insertion order, as in `dfs()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str, None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The starting node, as an integer ID or a string label. If `None` (default), search\n    from every unvisited node in turn.\n\n<code>[depth_limit]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Do not go deeper than this many hops from the start of each tree. Nodes at the limit\n    are still listed (NetworkX's `dfs_postorder_nodes()` omits them, unlike its\n    preorder). If `None` (default), there is no limit.\n\n<code>[mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Which way to follow edges on a directed graph: `\"out\"` (default), `\"in\"`, or\n    `\"all\"`. Ignored for undirected graphs.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Node IDs in postorder.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the node does not exist, `depth_limit=` is negative, or `mode=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~dfs`) \n\n:   The nodes in the order the search first visits them.\n\n[](`~topological_sort`) \n\n:   An order of a DAG with every edge pointing forward.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn a small tree, the leaves finish first and the root last:\n\n::: {#51065cf7 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ntree = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"root\", \"a\"), (\"root\", \"b\"), (\"a\", \"a1\"), (\"a\", \"a2\")],\n    directed=True,\n)\n\n[tree.get_label_from_id(n) for n in tree.dfs_postorder_nodes(\"root\")]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['a1', 'a2', 'a', 'b', 'root']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nReversing the postorder of a DAG gives a valid topological order:\n\n::: {#1c4c5c09 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\norder = list(reversed(tree.dfs_postorder_nodes()))\nposition = {n: i for i, n in enumerate(order)}\nall(position[s] < position[t] for _, s, t in tree.get_edges_as_tuples())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### An order to take the courses in\n\n`courses()` links each course of a made-up degree program to the courses that require it.\nA course finishes only after every course that needs it, so the reversed postorder puts\neach course after its prerequisites:\n\n::: {#0a070bf3 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses = ec.courses()\norder = list(reversed(courses.dfs_postorder_nodes()))\n\n[courses.get_label_from_id(n) for n in order]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n['MATH150',\n 'MATH101',\n 'MATH102',\n 'MATH210',\n 'STAT201',\n 'CS101',\n 'CS102',\n 'CS250',\n 'CS350',\n 'CS220',\n 'CS210',\n 'CS320',\n 'CS310',\n 'CS410',\n 'CS201',\n 'CS360',\n 'CS460']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#9755fd25 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncourses.set_node_attrs(\n    \"taken\", {n: i for i, n in enumerate(order, start=1)}\n)\ncourses.plot(\n    color_by=\"taken\", color_scale=\"sequential\", label_by=\"label\", seed=2\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-ff6c91af:#244d83;--ect-ff1ea111:#1c447a;--ect-c26f65a1:#77a6de;--ect-f572b836:#4f7bb3;--ect-7e8fe88c:#6694cd;--ect-5ee57d66:#4874ab;--ect-d06136e8:#5f8cc5;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-73a00b98:#3a649b;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-764eb3cb:#2b548b;--ect-d29233f2:#143d72;--ect-5dd4fa0a:#5683bb;--ect-fd7dd8f9:#7eaee7;--ect-8133927f:#416ca3;--ect-bedcb8ea:#6e9cd5;--ect-eb0fa70b:#325c92;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-6826a5f9:#608ec6;--ect-9d43aea2:#5480b8;--ect-3c980f0e:#3c679e;--ect-ec386ef0:#305a91;--ect-97f76ec5:#254e84;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-1b75f7cc:#19355b;--ect-806d374d:#132f55;--ect-7ac0b982:#53749b;--ect-a5899a45:#37567d;--ect-8a54ada3:#47678f;--ect-17801347:#325177;--ect-63d20321:#426289;--ect-bf50105f:#09254a;--ect-1bcffdb4:#28466c;--ect-6970a796:#5d7fa7;--ect-06730740:#1e3a61;--ect-7e01d800:#0e2a4f;--ect-55d85fd9:#3c5b82;--ect-f991b38f:#5879a1;--ect-3838da4c:#2d4b72;--ect-41288e7c:#4d6d95;--ect-47a5e22d:#234066;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: d